From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: in a virtual desktop only the window in front takes the X keyboard focus

X11DRV_SetFocus gave the X focus -- and the top -- to the window of any
program that moved its focus, the one behind too: clicking Notepad under the
Registry Editor, the Registry Editor moved the focus between its panes as it
was deactivated and took the keyboard and the top back (David, 2026-10-18).
---
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
@@ -1395,6 +1395,19 @@
         release_win_data( data );
         hwnd = parent;
     }
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_BACKGROUND_FOCUS
+    /* Stained Glass: in a virtual desktop only the window in front takes the
+     * X keyboard focus (and comes up with it). A program behind that moved
+     * the focus among its own windows -- the Registry Editor between its panes
+     * as it was deactivated -- took the keyboard and the top back from the
+     * window just clicked: Notepad active but under it, its keys going to the
+     * Registry Editor (David, 2026-10-18) */
+    if (is_virtual_desktop() && !data->embedder && hwnd != NtUserGetForegroundWindow())
+    {
+        release_win_data( data );
+        return;
+    }
+#endif
     if (!data->managed || data->embedder) set_input_focus( data );
     release_win_data( data );
 }
